# Distributed Job Scheduler

A CLI-based scheduler tool to initiate HTTP health-check jobs and (in progress) remote script execution — built to replace a proprietary scheduler tool.

## What This Is

Many teams rely on manual or proprietary tools to run scheduled health checks and scripts, which often come with licensing costs and limited flexibility. This project is a lightweight, open-source scheduler that lets users define HTTP jobs and (soon) remote script execution jobs, reducing manual operational effort.

## Tech Stack

- **Go** — core application logic
- **Cobra** — CLI framework
- **gRPC** — for remote job execution (in progress)
- **PostgreSQL** — job storage (URLs, cron schedules, notification settings)

## Key Features

- Add jobs via CLI, specifying the URL to monitor, a cron schedule, and an email address for failure notifications
- Job configuration is persisted in PostgreSQL and executed automatically at the scheduled time
- Failure notifications sent via email when a job's HTTP check fails
- **In progress:** remote script execution on other servers via gRPC

## Challenges & What I Learned

I started this project with no prior Go experience, using it as an opportunity to learn the language hands-on. It grew out of a real problem I'd seen at work — replacing a proprietary Windows Task Scheduler setup that had real limitations around flexibility and visibility into failures.

Building this taught me:
- How to structure a CLI application using the Cobra framework
- How to implement scheduled/cron-based job execution in Go
- How to send failure notifications over HTTP
- I'm currently learning gRPC in order to extend the scheduler to execute jobs on remote servers — this is the active area of development

## How to Run It

⚠️ Not yet packaged as a compiled binary. To run it locally:

- Clone the project and setup the tool , add the http jobs from cli and run the scheduler.

 https://github.com/pradeepshunmugam/scheduler.git


## Status

🚧 Actively in development — HTTP job scheduling is functional; remote job execution via gRPC is in progress.